## Preconditions

Do not deploy until required PR checks pass, the reviewed commit is on the intended branch, the promotion archive and SHA-256 exist, the target GitHub environment is configured, and the accountable human authorizes that environment.

## Preview

Run `Deploy preview` manually with the successful quality-run ID, full commit SHA, expected archive digest, and a validated isolated Worker name. Preview credentials must be separate from production. Treat preview content and URLs as public.

## Staging

Promote the same archive with `Deploy staging`. Verify the digest before extraction. Confirm primary pages, contact-route safe failure behavior, security headers, console errors, responsive layouts, and no unexpected external requests.

## Production

Run `Deploy production` only from `main`. The workflow verifies that the requested commit belongs to `main`, downloads the tested archive, checks its digest, and deploys under the production environment gate. It does not rebuild.

## Verification and evidence

Run `Post-deploy verification` against the exact HTTPS URL. Record workflow URLs, commit SHA, archive digest, approver, result, and any incident ID. Never record credentials or submitted contact data.

## Stop conditions

Stop on a missing approval, missing or mismatched digest, failing required check, unknown commit, unavailable rollback access, unexpected secret request, failed header check, or unhealthy customer path.

## Activation note

These workflows are definitions only until GitHub environments, secrets, required checks, and Cloudflare tokens are configured. This task did not deploy.
